implementationPlan.description:
Labels and comments only. Do not change behaviour, error handling or any fixture.

First record the baseline: `cd packages/moe-daemon && npx vitest run src/tools/qaApprove.test.ts src/state/deliveryProjection.test.ts`. Note the passed-test count.

1. packages/moe-daemon/src/tools/qaApprove.test.ts:1451, test title. Replace the stale reason with a real source of a padded record, e.g. 'accepts a pass recorded with a padded qualityGate, as an older wrapper or a direct record_check_run caller can record it'.
2. Its comment at 1452-1454 should say:
   - a hand-edited project.json can pad the gate;
   - both wrappers now trim it before running and recording (task-8fc35d31, f1399a3);
   - a padded record can still come from runs recorded before that fix, from an older wrapper an IDE plugin still bundles, or from a direct moe.record_check_run call (state/checkRunStore.ts keeps `command` as sent);
   - no shell sees the padding, so the run is the gate the policy requires.
3. packages/moe-daemon/src/state/deliveryProjection.test.ts:232, case label. For example: 'a runner-observed pass of the gate, padded as a pre-fix or direct record_check_run report carries it'.

Keep the `padded` value, the `{ command: ... }` inputs and every assertion byte-identical. Both files are LF; keep it that way.
